2026-10-15 03:02:34,734 DEBUG: Chroma query output: {'ids': [['sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_13', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_16', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_14', 'sluPolicy_cellPolicy_8', 'sluPolicy_tailgating_18', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_1', 'sluPolicy_artificial_intelligence_5', 'sluPolicy_cellPolicy_18']], 'embeddings': None, 'documents': [['. Prohibited Use of AI • AI cannot be given access to PII, specific information about tangible or real property, proprietary information, confidential data, restricted data, or any information that would otherwise undermine the cybersecurity or physical security of the university unless it is reviewed by the university ERP committee', '. It is the responsibility of the user to review the accuracy and ownership of any AI generated content. Academic Integrity For guidance on how AI intersects with academic honesty, it is recommended that instructors contact the Center for Faculty Excellence and review the Academic Integrity Policy. Be aware that AI detection tools are not always accurate and may produce false positives or miss certain cases', '. In general, student records subject to FERPA, health information subject to HIPAA, financial information subject to GLBA, proprietary information (such as intellectual property and system credentials), and any other information that could be considered protected university data must not be used with any AI without ERP review. • AI may not be used for any activity that would be illegal, fraudulent or a violation of any state or federal law, or Southeastern policies', '. DEPARTMENT HEAD: Assures subordinates’ compliance with the University Cellular Phone Policy. Certifies that conditions which justified issuance of a cellular telephone or payment of a stipend still exist. Exclusion Any exceptions to this policy must be requested in writing through administrative channels to the President. Questions Questions regarding this policy should be directed to Telephone Services', '. • Please note that signage will not be placed marking reservation spots. Fans are required to mark their own space for game day once approved. • Only the President of the student organization can request to reserve a green student organization tailgating spot. • Students/Fans who submit a request will receive a text message when their spot has been requested, approved or denied. • Students/Fans must request a spot for each individual game', '. Publicly available applications driven by AI, including generative AI that includes large language models (LLMs), chatbots, or image generators, are widely popular. This policy highlights the unique issues raised by AI, helps employees understand the guidelines for its acceptable use, and protects the university’s confidential information, intellectual property, culture, commitment to diversity, and brand', '. This includes, but is not limited to, student records subject to FERPA, health information subject to HIPAA, financial information subject to GLBA, proprietary information (such as intellectual property and system credentials), and any other information that could be considered protected university data. ERP Committee: The ERP committee is appointed by the President to lead in Enterprise Resource Planning for the university', '. I understand that I may be subject to disciplinary action for violation of this policy']], 'uris': None, 'included': ['metadatas', 'documents', 'distances'], 'data': None, 'metadatas': [[{'originFile': '/mnt/nvme0n1/database/storage/sluPolicy/readReady/artificial_intelligence.txt', 'index': 13, 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docContext': 'sluPolicy'}, {'docSource': 'https://www.southeastern.edu/resources/policies/policy_detail/artificial-intelligence-policy/', 'docContext': 'sluPolicy', 'index': 16, 'docName': 'Artificial Intelligence Policy', 'originFile'